<title>USA: Texaco shareholders vote against proposals.</title>
<headline>Texaco shareholders vote against proposals.</headline>
<dateline>RYE BROOK, N.Y. 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Texaco Inc shareholders rejected calls for diversity in the board of directors, an annual vote on the board's composition and the establishment of a shareholder advisory committee.</p>
<p>The oil major's chief executive Peter Bijur told shareholders that just 5.1 percent of shareholders had voted for an item demanding an advisory board, that 44.6 percent had voted for a yearly vote on the board and just 11.9 percent had voted in favor of racial diversity on the board.</p>
</text>
